  "reply_text": "Found one merge-blocking bug in `tag-cloud` (`89f074f`) against `main`:\n\n**[P1] `topTags` mutates the shared input array — `src/tags.js:10`**\n`tags.sort(...)` reorders the caller’s array in place, violating the documented non-mutating contract. Since `sidebar()` builds the cloud before taking `tags.slice(0, 5)`, the “recent” strip becomes the five highest-count tags rather than the first five supplied.\n\nConfirmed with six tags: the sixth input tag appears in `recent`, while the first disappears.\n\nSuggested fix: sort a copy (`[...tags].sort(...)`). Add regression tests asserting that `topTags` preserves input order and `sidebar().recent` matches the original first five tags.\n\nAll 4 existing tests pass, but they miss this regression. No files changed.",
